lesson k-round-letters v=1 format=teach grade=0 unit=9 subject=writing levels=[easy, medium, hard] {
  title "Letters that start with c"
  goal "Write c and the letters that start with a c shape, and tell d from b by how each one starts."

  look {
    scene 30x8 {
      handwriting rules show="c a d o g" rows=1 trace=1 width=26 at=canvas(1, 1)
    }
    say """
      c starts near the top and goes back round, the other way from a clock. a, d, o and g all start
      with that same c shape, and then add a little more: a stick for a and d, a join for o, and a
      tail for g.
      """
  }
  do {
    show k.c-for-cat x="c"
    level easy {
      worked k.c-shape-start k=0 level=medium
    }
    practice k.c-shape-start count=2 seed=2
    show k.trace-round x="o"
    practice k.first-move count=2 seed=4
    practice k.tall-or-small count=2 seed=5 easy-count=1
    show k.c-for-cat x="d"
  }
  try stars=2 {
    show k.b-or-d k=0 hard-k=1
  }
  try stars=3 {
    show k.round-in-a-word w="dog" easy-w="pig" hard-w="duck"
  }
  remember {
    say "c, a, d, o and g all start with the same c shape."
  }

  grown-ups """
    The traced rows are for you to look at: watch that the pencil goes back round to the left at
    the start of each letter, since a c drawn clockwise turns into a reversed letter later. b and d
    are the pair to watch, and the rule that helps is that d starts with a c. If the child is stuck,
    make the c shape together with a finger on the table before picking up the pencil. Off the
    page, write c-shape letters in a tray of rice or salt. England, Reception, ELG Writing: "Write
    recognisable letters, most of which are correctly formed".
    """
  level easy {
    grown-ups "At this level the first c-shape letter is found in the teacher's pen, the letters to judge are round ones and l, and the three-star's word is pig."
  }
  level hard {
    grown-ups "At this level the c-shape letters to find are d and g, the letters to judge include t, the two-star asks about p and q, and the three-star's word is duck."
  }
}
